# Shell scripts must reach `bash` with LF. `core.autocrlf=true` is a per-machine setting, so without this line a
# checkout on a machine that smudges CRLF gives every script here a `\r` on each line — and `bash scripts/…sh` fails
# on line 1 with no mention of line endings. The four tracked scripts are all LF today, so pinning them is a
# no-op locally and a guarantee on a fresh clone (D33: the fresh-clone path is the one nobody walks).
*.sh text eol=lf
